# Canonical identity for this repo's history.
#
# One 2020 commit (ed0b315) was authored and committed as
# "Ben's laptop <ruubixo@gmail.com>" from a personal alt address. Everything
# else already uses the canonical address.
#
# This maps it for `git log`, `git shortlog`, `git blame` and forge UIs with no
# rewrite. Rewriting the object instead would touch ed0b315 and all 285 commits
# after it — invalidating every SHA in the repo, including the ones the
# PROVENANCE notes reference. Not worth it for a tidiness issue.
#
# The stored commit object still holds the old address, so
# `git log --format=%ae` continues to show it. Escalate to
# `git filter-repo --mailmap` only if the stored value itself has to change,
# e.g. before making the repo public.
#
# Format: Canonical Name <canonical@email> Commit Name <commit@email>

Ben Davis <bengineerdavis@gmail.com> Ben's laptop <ruubixo@gmail.com>
